{
  "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
  "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Richard D. Friedman",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We ask the Court in this case to take no new ground beyond that established just last term in the Melendez-Diaz case, but the stakes of this case are high. If the Court were to reverse Melendez-Diaz and hold that a State may impose on the defendant the burden of calling a prosecution witness to the stand, it would severely impair the confrontation right and threaten a fundamental transformation in the way Anglo-American trials have been conducted for hundreds of years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is that overruling Melendez-Diaz?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's not clear to me what your answer to these questions is. If all the prosecution does is call the analyst on the stand and admit -- have the analyst provide a foundation for the admission of the report, let's say, pursuant to the hearsay exception for recorded recollection, and does nothing more, would there be a Confrontation Clause problem?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What happens if the lab is -- is divided into four or five parts and there is several different machines and we have different people at different times using these different machines and performing different operations and each, at the end, certifies that the red light was on or it was this or it was that? Now, do we have to call all those people?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. FRIEDMAN",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The prosecution has to present the testimony of witnesses. It has to present the testimony live. Depending on how the lab is organized -- usually, labs can organize so that only one person needs to -- needs to present."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, does that square with where we started out? We have situation A, where the prosecutor calls the lab analyst, and the lab analyst says, this is my report, and I stand by it, period. Now, it's up to the defense to cross-examine. That's situation A."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. FRIEDMAN",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't believe it's cross-examination. In practice, it is -- if the defendant said, I don't want to cross-examine, but I still insist that the witness get up on the stand and let's see what the witness can do -- and the Commonwealth makes no attempt to distinguish between these witnesses and other witnesses for what is -- what is satisfactory confrontation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, the problem you describe, the hearsay rule would have solved that alone, wouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McCullough (Commonwealth)",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCULLOUGH: Under both the plain language of the statute and the way it\u2019s been construed adversely to the Commonwealth. The plain language of the statute is the witness shall be summoned and appear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: No, we\u2019re not going in circles at all. You -- you appeal to the language that the witness shall appear as resolving what happens when he doesn't, and it doesn't resolve that. It just says he must appear. And if he doesn't appear, what happens?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It went into effect August 21, 2009."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Leondra R. Kruger (Amicus Curiae for United States)",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KRUGER: Our principal submission is that the Confrontation Clause allows the government to rely on affidavits, so long as it bring the affiants into court, so that the defendant can ask whatever questions --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Commonwealth",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Many defendants did that, including Grant, the defendant on whom -- in the case on whom the Commonwealth relies so heavily. The prosecution ignored those requests."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Commonwealth",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No court has ever held -- no court has ever held in Virginia that the prosecution bears the risk of -- of no-shows."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Commonwealth and United States",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Commonwealth and the United States suggest: Oh, it's okay to -- to transform the way trials are conducted by allowing the prosecution to present affidavits because you can backfill with the Due Process Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I take it your position is it wouldn't matter. If the -- if Virginia said that the -- the Commonwealth bears the risk of a no-show, that wouldn't make any difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would you like us to grant, vacate, and remand in this case and say because it's unclear who has the risk of a no-show?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think Melendez-Diaz addressed the question of the order of proof? Where did it address that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So is the proper solution to grant, vacate, and remand in light of Melendez-Diaz?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "9f3e58830a8d38c46ce7d79bfa385d99212a415b756cf9424de9058e8321f531",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9f3e58830a8d-0003-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-07-11191",
      "confidence": 0.0,
